  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This FM broadcast captures the Mountain Goats performing an intimate eight-song set on Saturday, 27 March 2004, at the VPRO DAWRS Session Studio DeSmet in Amsterdam [1][2]. The recording, which runs for thirty-five minutes, was taped by straap and later transferred to digital formats, with the lineage documented as cable FM to minidisc, then hard drive, WAV, and finally FLAC [1]. The setlist features four songs that are the only archived performances available for them, including “Jingle,” “New World Merging Blues,” and “DJ Closing” [1][2]. Additionally, the group plays “Going To Cleveland,” which is rare with only eight archived performances, and “The Boys Are Back In Town,” which has five archived performances [1][2]. The remaining tracks are “Cotton” and “Your Belgian Things” [1]. The session includes spoken introductions and stories about the song “DJ” [1]. This performance is the fifty-seventh of 467 archived shows for the band, following a previous recording from 3 March 2004 at the Knitting Factory [2]. The broadcast was originally aired on 30 September 2004 [1].",
